<%# One remembered create, shown in the flat list it would have joined.
    #
    # This is deliberately **not** the list row partial with its controls switched
    # off, because there is nothing to switch: a remembered create names no record
    # (ADR 0019), so it has no id for a details link, no URL for an editor, and no
    # position for the ordering a sibling list maintains. It is read rather than
    # operated on — the way into it is the drafts page, which is what the panel in
    # the right sidebar and the **Pending changes** entry both lead to.
    #
    # The values are the ones the payload carries, so a row shows what the author
    # submitted — its name, its description, and the tags and photo they gave it.
    # `DraftPreview` assigns the submitted tags onto the record and holds the photo
    # beside it, so the tag badges here are the same `entity_tag_badge` a live row
    # prints and the photo is the shared pending thumbnail.
    #
    # The subject is `draft_pending_record_label`, not `record_label`, because a
    # remembered create is not validated and may be a record the universe would
    # refuse — and one with nothing to be called by would otherwise print a
    # placeholder id or no subject at all. The fallback is the type it would
    # create, which is the same sentence the drafts page gives that change. %>
<div class="list-group-item entity-row draft-pending-row d-flex align-items-center gap-3">
  <%= render "shared/draft_pending_photo",
    photo_data: draft_pending_photo(record), name: draft_pending_record_label(record) %>

  <div class="entity-copy flex-grow-1">
    <div class="d-flex align-items-center gap-2 flex-wrap">
      <span class="entity-title text-break"><%= draft_pending_record_label(record) %></span>
      <%= entity_tag_badge(record) %>
      <%= render "shared/draft_pending_badge", record: record %>
    </div>
    <% if record.description.present? %>
      <div class="entity-description"><%= record.description %></div>
    <% end %>
  </div>
</div>